    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d46">

                <pb facs="0082" n="28" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg28"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President
                        Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d46-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-01">1 September 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 777. Prime Minister to President Roosevelt. Personal and top secret.</p>
                <p>I hope you will pardon a further transgression of the Teheran scale. I am going
                    to bring Mrs. Churchill with me.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d46-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d46-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Washington by the United States Military Attaché, London, via Army
                    channels; forwarded by the White House Map Room to Roosevelt, who was at Hyde
                    Park, as telegram No. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Red</hi> 348.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
